From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: GetCurrentPackageInfo2/3, GetPackageInfo[2], OpenPackageInfoByFullName, ClosePackageInfo

The Windows App SDK runtime (Microsoft.WindowsAppRuntime.dll) hooks the
package graph functions in its DllMain for an unpackaged program: on
Windows 10 19H1 and later it looks up GetCurrentPackageInfo2 and
GetPackageInfo2 from api-ms-win-appmodel-runtime-l1-1-3, and on 20H1 and
later GetCurrentPackageInfo3 from api-ms-win-appmodel-runtime-internal-l1-1-6,
and stops the process (c0000409) when one is missing. They were missing, as
were GetPackageInfo, OpenPackageInfoByFullName[ForUser] and ClosePackageInfo.
They now give the package graph GetCurrentPackageInfo gives (the package,
then its frameworks), for the current package or a deployed one by name,
with the path kind asked for.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
index b9c5e61..47d429b 100644
--- a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
@@ -225,6 +225,7 @@
 @ stdcall -import ClearCommError(long ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall CloseConsoleHandle(long)
 @ stdcall -import CloseHandle(long)
+@ stdcall ClosePackageInfo(ptr) kernelbase.ClosePackageInfo
 @ stdcall -import ClosePrivateNamespace(long long)
 @ stdcall CloseProfileUserMapping()
 @ stdcall -import ClosePseudoConsole(ptr)
@@ -642,6 +643,7 @@
 @ stdcall GetCurrentPackageFullName(ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetCurrentPackageFullName
 @ stdcall GetCurrentPackageId(ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetCurrentPackageId
 @ stdcall GetCurrentPackageInfo(long ptr ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetCurrentPackageInfo
+@ stdcall GetCurrentPackageInfo2(long long ptr ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetCurrentPackageInfo2
 @ stdcall GetCurrentPackagePath(ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetCurrentPackagePath
 @ stdcall -norelay GetCurrentProcess() KERNEL32_GetCurrentProcess
 @ stdcall -norelay GetCurrentProcessId() KERNEL32_GetCurrentProcessId
@@ -783,6 +785,8 @@
 @ stdcall -import GetUserPreferredUILanguages(long ptr ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall GetPackageFamilyName(long ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetPackageFamilyName
 @ stdcall GetPackageFullName(long ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetPackageFullName
+@ stdcall GetPackageInfo(ptr long ptr ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetPackageInfo
+@ stdcall GetPackageInfo2(ptr long long ptr ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetPackageInfo2
 @ stdcall GetPackagesByPackageFamily(wstr ptr ptr ptr ptr) kernelbase.GetPackagesByPackageFamily
 @ stdcall GetPackagePathByFullName(wstr ptr wstr) kernelbase.GetPackagePathByFullName
 @ stdcall -import GetPhysicallyInstalledSystemMemory(ptr)
@@ -1159,6 +1163,7 @@
 @ stdcall OpenJobObjectW(long long wstr)
 @ stdcall OpenMutexA(long long str)
 @ stdcall -import OpenMutexW(long long wstr)
+@ stdcall OpenPackageInfoByFullName(wstr long ptr) kernelbase.OpenPackageInfoByFullName
 @ stdcall OpenPrivateNamespaceA(ptr str)
 @ stdcall -import OpenPrivateNamespaceW(ptr wstr)
 @ stdcall -import OpenProcess(long long long)
